import UnforcedLeray.Short.PartIIb.Defs

/-!
# Part II-b, task `PartII-b:T11`: uniqueness of the flat response (conditional)

Source of record: `the November 2 reference manuscript`. The statement is the
"free uniqueness" used at lines 2328, 2618 and 3575 (and the clause "exactly one flat response" of
`ProfileGraphFlat`, `StatementsFree.lean`, SP 1921-1938, where the causal formula
`T_0F(s) = ∫_0^s (t/s)^μ e^{ν(s-t)Δ} P_0F(t) dt/t` of line 1924 defines `T_0`). The source never
writes the uniqueness proof, and the energy identity of lines 1684-1690 is only the Hilbert case
`r = 2`; the argument below works for every `1 < r < 3`.

## Mathematical proof (duality with the backward heat flow; no energy estimate)

Let `b` be in the flat class with `(μ + S - νsΔ_{q,η}) b = 0` against planar solenoidal tests and
`a_r = Re μ + (3/r - 1)/2 > 0`.

1. (*Streams.*) Planar solenoidal tests are generated by `Ψ = ∇^⊥ψ = (∂_ηψ, -∂_qψ)`, and the
   equation commutes with `∇^⊥`. By periodicity of `b` in `q` the equation extends to
   `q`-periodic streams `ψ` with compact support in `(s, η)` (`FlatEqCellStream`: partition of
   unity `Σ_n θ(q - nc) = 1`; the commutator terms telescope since `Σ_n θ'(q - nc) = 0`).
2. (*Dual solution.*) Let `ζ` be a nice stream (smooth, `c`-periodic in `q`, compact in `η`),
   `H(τ)` its forward heat flow `H_τ = νΔH`, and for `s > 0` put `g(σ) = H(s - σ)`, so that
   `g_σ + νΔg = 0` on `0 < σ < s`. For `a(σ) = χ(σ)σ^{μ-1}` with `χ ∈ C_c^∞(0, s)`,
   `Tψ := (μ-1)ψ - σψ_σ - νσΔψ` with `ψ = a g` equals `-χ'(σ)σ^μ g`. Testing with
   `ψ = a(σ) φ_L(η) g` (real and imaginary parts separately; `φ_L` an `η`-cutoff; the cutoff
   errors are `O(1/L)` by Hölder, `b ∈ L^r`, derivatives of `g` in `L^{r'}`) gives
   `∫ χ'(σ) F(σ) dσ = 0` for all `χ`, where
   `F(σ) = σ^μ ∫ b(σ)·∇^⊥g(σ) dq dη/c` (`FlatDualConstancy`): `F = κ` a.e. on `(0, s)`.
3. (*Zero entrance.*) `|F(σ)| ≤ σ^{Re μ}‖b(σ)‖_{L^r} ‖∇^⊥H‖_{L^{r'}}` (heat contraction on `L^{r'}`)
   `= σ^{a_r} · (σ^{1/2-3/(2r)}‖b(σ)‖_{L^r}) · C`. Since
   `∫_0^1 (σ^{1/2-3/(2r)}‖b(σ)‖_r)^r dσ/σ = ‖b‖_{H_r}^r < ∞` (this is `H_r` membership), the
   slice quantity is `≤ ε` on a set of positive measure near `0` (`SmallSliceNorm`), so `κ = 0`
   because `a_r > 0`.
4. (*Return to the initial datum.*) For each `s`, `⟨b(σ), ∇^⊥H(s-σ)⟩ = 0` for a.e. `σ < s`; with
   `s - σ → 0` the heat flow tends to `ζ` in `L^{r'}`, and averaging in `s` against an approximate
   identity gives `∫ θ(σ) ⟨b(σ), ∇^⊥ζ⟩ dσ = 0` (`FlatSliceOrthogonality`).
5. (*Separation.*) A weakly solenoidal `b ∈ H_r` with `curl b = 0` against all nice streams is
   zero (`NiceFieldsSeparate`: after mollification `b_1 - i b_2` is holomorphic, `c`-periodic and in
   `L^r(cell × ℝ)`, so the area mean value property gives `|f(z)| ≤ C R^{-2/r}(R/c+1)^{1/r}‖f‖_r → 0`).

Proved here: the glue `flat_unique_of` from `FlatSliceOrthogonality` (leaf `PartII-b:T11/5`) and
`NiceFieldsSeparate` (leaf `PartII-b:T11/6`). The leaves `FlatEqCellStream` (`T11/1`),
`FlatDualConstancy` (`T11/2`), `HeatStreamDual` (`T11/3`), `SmallSliceNorm` (`T11/4`) are the
ingredients of `T11/5`; they are stated with exact Lean types so the drafters have precise targets.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

open Set MeasureTheory Filter Topology
open scoped ENNReal ContDiff

namespace UnforcedLeray.Short.IIb

/-- `∇^⊥ζ = (∂_ηζ, -∂_qζ)` of a scalar stream on the plane `(q, η)`. -/
def perpGrad (ζ : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ) (p : ℝ × ℝ) : Fin 2 → ℝ :=
  ![fderiv ℝ ζ p (0, 1), -fderiv ℝ ζ p (1, 0)]

/-- A *nice stream*: smooth, `c`-periodic in `q`, vanishing for `|η|` large. Its `∇^⊥` is a
`c`-periodic, planar solenoidal, `η`-compact field. -/
structure NiceStream (c : ℝ) (ζ : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ) : Prop where
  smooth : ContDiff ℝ ∞ ζ
  periodic : ∀ p : ℝ × ℝ, ζ (p.1 + c, p.2) = ζ p
  compact : ∃ L : ℝ, ∀ p : ℝ × ℝ, L ≤ |p.2| → ζ p = 0

/-- A time cutoff: smooth with compact support in `(0, ∞)`. -/
structure TimeTest (θ : ℝ → ℝ) : Prop where
  smooth : ContDiff ℝ ∞ θ
  compact : HasCompactSupport θ
  supp : tsupport θ ⊆ Ioi (0 : ℝ)

/-- The integrand `b · (θ(s) ∇^⊥ζ(q, η))` of the pairing of a profile with a product test. -/
def streamPair (b : CProf) (θ : ℝ → ℝ) (ζ : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ) (x : Coord) : ℂ :=
  ∑ i : Fin 2, b x i * ((θ x.1 * perpGrad ζ x.2 i : ℝ) : ℂ)

/-- A smooth solution `H(τ, q, η)` of the forward heat equation `H_τ = ν Δ_{q,η} H` for `τ > 0`
(first coordinate of `Coord` is `τ`), `c`-periodic in `q`, whose partial derivatives of order
`≤ 3` in all variables are in `L^{r'}` of `[τ₁, τ₂] × cell × ℝ_η` for `0 < τ₁ ≤ τ₂`. -/
structure HeatSol (c ν r' : ℝ) (H : Coord → ℝ) : Prop where
  smooth : ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ H (Ioi (0 : ℝ) ×ˢ (univ : Set (ℝ × ℝ)))
  periodic : ∀ x : Coord, 0 < x.1 → H (qShift c x) = H x
  heat : ∀ x ∈ Ioi (0 : ℝ) ×ˢ (univ : Set (ℝ × ℝ)),
    cpd 0 H x = ν * (cpd 1 (cpd 1 H) x + cpd 2 (cpd 2 H) x)
  deriv_memLp : ∀ n : ℕ, n ≤ 3 → ∀ τ₁ τ₂ : ℝ, 0 < τ₁ → τ₁ ≤ τ₂ →
    MemLp (fun x => iteratedFDeriv ℝ n H x) (ENNReal.ofReal r')
      ((Axi.ageμ c 0).restrict (Icc τ₁ τ₂ ×ˢ (univ : Set (ℝ × ℝ))))

/-- **Leaf `PartII-b:T11/1`** (periodic stream tests; SP 1923-1927 flat equation). If `b ∈ H_r` is a
flat response to `0`, the equation `∫ b · flatTranspose(Ψ) = 0` also holds for
`Ψ = ∇^⊥ψ` with `ψ` smooth, `c`-periodic in `q` and compactly supported in `(s, η)` inside
`s > 0`, the integral being taken over the cell (`ageμ c 0 = ds ⊗ dq/c dη|_cell`, `s > 0`).
Proof: for `θ` with `Σ_n θ(q - nc) = 1`, `θψ` is a legitimate test; `∇^⊥(θψ)` differs from `θ∇^⊥ψ`
by terms linear in `θ', θ''` with periodic coefficients, which integrate to `0` over the cell
because `Σ_n θ'(· - nc) = Σ_n θ''(· - nc) = 0`; unfold `∫_ℝ θ f = ∫_cell f` for periodic `f`.
Integrability of the cell integrand comes from `b ∈ L^r(s^{r/2-5/2} ds)`. -/
def FlatEqCellStream : Prop :=
  ∀ (c r ν : ℝ) (μ : ℂ) (b : CProf), 0 < c → 0 < ν → 1 < r → InHr c r b →
    IsFlatResponse ν μ 0 b →
    ∀ ψ : Coord → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ ∞ ψ → (∀ x, ψ (qShift c x) = ψ x) →
      (∃ σ H L : ℝ, 0 < σ ∧ ∀ x : Coord, (x.1 < σ ∨ H < x.1 ∨ L < |x.2.2|) → ψ x = 0) →
      ∫ x, ∑ i : Fin 2, b x i * flatTranspose ν μ (fun y => ![cpd 2 ψ y, -cpd 1 ψ y]) x i
          ∂(Axi.ageμ c 0) = 0

/-- **Leaf `PartII-b:T11/2`** (dual constancy; uses `T11/1`). For a flat response `b` to `0` in
`H_r` and a heat solution `H` (so `g(σ, ·) = H(s - σ, ·)` solves `g_σ + νΔg = 0` on `(0, s)`),
the function `σ ↦ σ^μ ∫ b(σ)·∇^⊥g(σ) dq dη/c` is a.e. constant on `(0, s)`.
Proof: test `T11/1` with `ψ = Re(a) φ_L g` and `ψ = Im(a) φ_L g`, `a = χ(σ)σ^{μ-1}`,
`χ ∈ C_c^∞(0, s)`, `φ_L(η) = φ(η/L)`. Since `g_σ = -νΔg`,
`(μ-1)a g - σ(a g)_σ - νσ a Δg = -χ'(σ)σ^μ g`; the `η`-cutoff commutator terms are bounded by
`C L^{-1} ‖b‖_{L^r} Σ_{|α|≤3}‖∂^α g‖_{L^{r'}}` (Hölder over `supp χ × cell × ℝ`), tending to `0`.
Then `∫ χ' F = 0` for all `χ` gives `F` a.e. constant (du Bois-Reymond; `F` is locally integrable
by Hölder). -/
def FlatDualConstancy : Prop :=
  ∀ (c r ν : ℝ) (μ : ℂ) (b : CProf) (H : Coord → ℝ) (s : ℝ),
    0 < c → 0 < ν → 1 < r → 0 < s → InHr c r b → IsFlatResponse ν μ 0 b →
    HeatSol c ν (r / (r - 1)) H →
    ∃ κ : ℂ, ∀ᵐ σ : ℝ ∂(volume.restrict (Ioo (0 : ℝ) s)),
      ((σ : ℝ) : ℂ) ^ μ * ∫ p, ∑ i : Fin 2, b (σ, p) i *
          ((perpGrad (fun z => H (s - σ, z)) p i : ℝ) : ℂ) ∂(Cyl.avgμ c) = κ

/-- **Leaf `PartII-b:T11/3`** (heat flow of a nice stream). For a nice stream `ζ` the cylinder heat
flow `H(τ) = e^{ντΔ}ζ` (planar Gaussian convolution of the `q`-periodization, or of the planar
compactly supported datum; heat kernel `(4πντ)^{-1} exp(-|x|²/(4ντ))`) is a `HeatSol` with
`L^{r'}`-contractive `∇^⊥H(τ)` (derivatives commute with convolution; Young/Minkowski on the cell,
`Lib/CylinderB/Periodize.lean`: `eLpNorm_planarConv_periodic_le`) and
`‖∇^⊥H(τ) - ∇^⊥ζ‖_{L^{r'}(cell)} → 0` as `τ → 0+` (approximate identity, `Lib/Kernels`/
`Lib/HeatCylinder`). Derivative integrability: Gaussian tails against the `η`-compact datum. -/
def HeatStreamDual : Prop :=
  ∀ (c ν r' : ℝ) (ζ : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ), 0 < c → 0 < ν → 1 < r' → NiceStream c ζ →
    ∃ H : Coord → ℝ, HeatSol c ν r' H ∧
      (∀ τ : ℝ, 0 < τ → ∀ i : Fin 2,
        ∫⁻ p, ‖perpGrad (fun z => H (τ, z)) p i‖ₑ ^ r' ∂(Cyl.avgμ c) ≤
          ∫⁻ p, ‖perpGrad ζ p i‖ₑ ^ r' ∂(Cyl.avgμ c)) ∧
      (∀ i : Fin 2, Tendsto
        (fun τ : ℝ => ∫⁻ p, ‖perpGrad (fun z => H (τ, z)) p i - perpGrad ζ p i‖ₑ ^ r'
          ∂(Cyl.avgμ c)) (𝓝[>] (0 : ℝ)) (𝓝 0))

/-- **Leaf `PartII-b:T11/4`** (zero entrance, a measure-theoretic consequence of `H_r`). If
`b ∈ H_r`, then for all `ε, σ₀ > 0` the set of ages `σ ∈ (0, σ₀)` with
`σ^{r/2-3/2} ∫|b(σ, ·)|^r dq/c dη ≤ ε` has positive measure. Proof: by Tonelli
`∫_0^∞ [σ^{r/2-3/2} ∫|b(σ)|^r] dσ/σ = ‖b‖_{H_r}^r < ∞`; if the bracket exceeded `ε` a.e. on
`(0, σ₀)`, the integral would be `≥ ε ∫_0^{σ₀} dσ/σ = ∞`. (Use an a.e.-measurable
representative of `b`; the bracket is then measurable in `σ`.) -/
def SmallSliceNorm : Prop :=
  ∀ (c r : ℝ) (b : CProf), 0 < c → 1 < r → InHr c r b →
    ∀ ε σ₀ : ℝ, 0 < ε → 0 < σ₀ →
      0 < (volume : Measure ℝ) {σ : ℝ | σ ∈ Ioo (0 : ℝ) σ₀ ∧
        ENNReal.ofReal (σ ^ (r / 2 - 3 / 2)) * ∫⁻ p, ‖b (σ, p)‖ₑ ^ r ∂(Cyl.avgμ c)
          ≤ ENNReal.ofReal ε}

/-- **Leaf `PartII-b:T11/5`** (slice orthogonality; uses `T11/1`-`T11/4`, SP 1923-1938 with `a_r > 0`).
For `b` in the flat class with flat response `0`, `b` is orthogonal to every product test
`θ(s) ∇^⊥ζ(q, η)` (`θ` a time cutoff, `ζ` a nice stream): the pairing integral over the cell vanishes.
Proof: `T11/3` gives `H`; `T11/2` gives `F(σ) = κ_s` on `(0, s)`; `T11/4` with
`|F(σ)| ≤ σ^{a_r}·ε^{1/r}·C` (Hölder on the slice, `C^{r'} = ‖∇^⊥ζ‖_{L^{r'}}^{r'}` by the contraction
bound; `Re μ = a_r - (3/r-1)/2`) forces `κ_s = 0`. So for every `s`: `⟨b(σ), ∇^⊥H(s-σ)⟩ = 0` for
a.e. `σ < s`. Multiply by `θ(σ)ρ_δ(s - σ)` (`ρ_δ ≥ 0` an approximate identity supported in
`(0, δ)`), integrate in `(σ, s)` (Fubini) and let `δ → 0` using the `L^{r'}` convergence of
`∇^⊥H(τ)` to `∇^⊥ζ` (dominated by `‖θ b‖_{L^1(L^r)} < ∞`). The integral is a genuine Bochner
integral: the integrand is integrable since `b ∈ L^r(s^{r/2-5/2} ds)` and the test is bounded with
compact support in `s` and `η`. -/
def FlatSliceOrthogonality : Prop :=
  ∀ (c r ν : ℝ) (μ : ℂ), 0 < c → 0 < ν → 1 < r → r < 3 → 0 < μ.re + (3 / r - 1) / 2 →
    ∀ b : CProf, InFlatClass c r b → IsFlatResponse ν μ 0 b →
      ∀ (θ : ℝ → ℝ) (ζ : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ), TimeTest θ → NiceStream c ζ →
        ∫ x, streamPair b θ ζ x ∂(Axi.ageμ c 0) = 0

/-- **Leaf `PartII-b:T11/6`** (separation by nice streams; SP 2618 context, 2D Liouville). A
profile `b ∈ H_r` (`1 < r < 3`) that is weakly planar solenoidal (the `solenoidal` clause of
`IsFlatResponse`, tested against compactly supported scalar tests) and orthogonal to all product
tests `θ(s) ∇^⊥ζ` vanishes `hMeas`-a.e.
Proof: periodize the compactly supported tests (`b` is `c`-periodic), so `div b = 0 = curl b` in
distributions on `{s > 0} × ℝ²`. Mollify in `(s, q, η)` with a tensor mollifier: `b_ρ` is smooth,
`c`-periodic in `q`, in `L^r(cell × ℝ)` on `s`-windows, and `f = (b_ρ)_r - i (b_ρ)_z`
satisfies Cauchy-Riemann in `q + iη`, so it is entire; the area mean value property over a disc
of radius `R` and Hölder give `|f(z)|^r ≤ C R^{-2}(R/c + 2) ‖f‖^r_{L^r(cell × ℝ)} → 0`. So
`b_ρ = 0` for all mollifiers `ρ`, whence `b = 0` a.e. (Lebesgue differentiation / approximate
identity; `Lib/CylinderB/Liouville*.lean` is the `L²`/Fourier-mode analogue and may be adapted.) -/
def NiceFieldsSeparate : Prop :=
  ∀ (c r : ℝ) (b : CProf), 0 < c → 1 < r → r < 3 → InHr c r b →
    (∀ φ : Coord → ℝ, IsCoordTest φ →
      Integrable (fun x => b x 0 * (cpd 1 φ x : ℂ) + b x 1 * (cpd 2 φ x : ℂ)) ∧
        ∫ x, (b x 0 * (cpd 1 φ x : ℂ) + b x 1 * (cpd 2 φ x : ℂ)) = 0) →
    (∀ (θ : ℝ → ℝ) (ζ : ℝ × ℝ → ℝ), TimeTest θ → NiceStream c ζ →
      ∫ x, streamPair b θ ζ x ∂(Axi.ageμ c 0) = 0) →
    b =ᵐ[hMeas c r] 0

/-- **Conditional flat uniqueness** (`PartII-b:T11`, target `flat_unique`): the exact statement of
-/
theorem flat_unique_of (h5 : FlatSliceOrthogonality) (h6 : NiceFieldsSeparate)
    {c r ν : ℝ} {μ : ℂ} (hc : 0 < c) (hν : 0 < ν) (hr : 1 < r) (hr3 : r < 3)
    (ha : 0 < μ.re + (3 / r - 1) / 2) (b : CProf) (hb : InFlatClass c r b)
    (h0 : IsFlatResponse ν μ 0 b) : b =ᵐ[hMeas c r] 0 :=
  h6 c r b hc hr hr3 hb.inHr h0.solenoidal
    (fun θ ζ hθ hζ => h5 c r ν μ hc hν hr hr3 ha b hb h0 θ ζ hθ hζ)

end UnforcedLeray.Short.IIb
